    "result_text": "All tests pass. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization applied whenever an owner is created (`POST /api/owners`).\n\n**New file \u2014 `AddressNormalizer.java`** (in `rest/function/owner/`): the single canonical normalizer. It trims, collapses whitespace runs to one space, upper-cases, and expands whole-word abbreviations `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. Empty/blank/`null` input normalizes to `\"\"`.\n\n**Wired it into the create pipeline at three points:**\n\n1. **`RequireOwnerFields`** \u2014 normalizes the address up-front and writes it back onto the request body *before* the required-field check. This makes the stored/returned address the normalized form, and makes the blank check reject an address that is empty only after normalization (e.g. `\"   \"` \u2192 `\"\"` \u2192 400).\n\n2. **`RequireUniqueHousehold`** \u2014 household duplicate detection now compares both the incoming and each existing owner's address through `AddressNormalizer`, so duplicates are matched on the normalized form (robust even for pre-existing un-normalized records).\n\n3. **`AssignHouseholdId`** \u2014 the shared `householdId` hash key now derives the address component from `AddressNormalizer`, keeping shared-household ids consistent with duplicate detection.\n\nSince the normalized address is written onto the request body, `BuildOwner`/`OwnerMapper` persist it and `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it (`\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`, `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`).\n\n**Tests:** the full suite (`AcceptanceTest`, 3 tests including the two normalization cases and the blank-after-normalize rejection) passes \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures.",
